{
  "id": "Compound::DB00451 - Gene::8140",
  "verbalization": "Levothyroxine is implicated in the pathogenesis of multiple conditions, including craniosynostosis, slipped femoral capital epiphysis, and epiphysiolysis, all of which are associated with Dextrothyroxine. These conditions are linked to the binding of Dextrothyroxine to Slc7a5, a transporter protein involved in thyroid hormone transport. The shared pathway involves Levothyroxine and Dextrothyroxine both being classified under the Thyroid Agent and Thyroxine ontologies, suggesting a functional or pharmacological relationship between these compounds and Slc7a5. The evidence points to a mechanism where Levothyroxine, through its interaction with Dextrothyroxine, may influence Slc7a5 expression or activity, potentially altering thyroid hormone homeostasis. This relationship is supported by the consistent binding of Dextrothyroxine to Slc7a5 across multiple conditions, reinforcing the role of Slc7a5 in thyroid hormone transport and its potential involvement in the pathogenesis of these disorders.",
